        "id": 18914
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-14T14:35:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay, I see what you mean. The BlendColorFilterBlock takes in a source color at block creation from PaintParams though, whereas the source color would need to come from the render step\u0027s SkSL (from RenderStep::fragmentColorSkSL(), which assigns to a `primitiveColor` variable).\n\nSuch that we get a block that can take in both a source color (primitive color from render step) and a dest color (priorStageOutput) for the blend.\n\nDoes that mean we would need the Args struct to store a fSrcColor as opposed to fDestColor, since fDestColor would be the prior-stage output? Or did I over-complicate it and think myself into a circle? 😊",
      "parentUuid": "1f4340df_4172a199",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 74,
        "startChar": 74,
