      "writtenOn": "2022-09-14T14:37:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What do you mean by \"The BlendColorFilterBlock takes in a source color at block creation from PaintParams\"?\n\nhttps://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:src/core/SkKeyHelpers.h;l\u003d196;drc\u003df172cd146979d4c67229c13afa0e5f6ea14738e9\n\nIt looks like it takes a `BlendColorFilterData` which lets you specify any blend-mode and color4f. I don\u0027t understand how it\u0027s tied to PaintParams.",
      "parentUuid": "4d0c3364_e6847da3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 74,
        "startChar": 74,
        "endLine": 74,
        "endChar": 81
      },
      "revId": "ca6652103b5a787457fcd311daeebe7c83f1d836",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bbf7b928_f68f6c2e",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/PaintParams.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 74,
      "author": {
        "id": 18914
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-14T15:13:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I mean that when I use `BlendColorFilterData::BeginBlock` from within `PaintParams::toKey` to capture the primitive blending step, I would need to create \u0026 pass in `BlendColorFilterData` containing both the blend mode (known, since paint params has access to the primitive blender as a member attribute) and a source color (not known at this point, since that will be determined by emitted information from the render step during `SkShaderCodeDictionary`\u0027s `SkShaderInfo::toSkSL`; `step-\u003efragmentColorSkSL()`). \n\nIs it a viable option to simply assign `BlendColorFilterData`\u0027s source color \"later\" from within the fragment shader?",
      "parentUuid": "029f790b_a503d2be",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 74,
        "startChar": 74,
        "endLine": 74,
        "endChar": 81
      },
      "revId": "ca6652103b5a787457fcd311daeebe7c83f1d836",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "08464ae9_c90ec148",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/PaintParams.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 74,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-15T18:58:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I needed to look at a diagram of the paint flow that Brian Salomon sent out a few months ago to fully understand the flow:\n \nhttps://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1vFlrDxBhAvygDeoyDlWLmOC6JQtp1wVlSXyq0LlUItA/edit?resourcekey\u003d0-VSsIdNzu-J4m5tJzbmKMrQ#slide\u003did.g10541deba55_0_255\n\nThe primitive blend step takes in as inputs:\n- \"S\": the output from the shader/paint-color stage (the \"priorStageOutput\")\n- \"D\": the \"primitive color\"\n- \"blend\": the blend mode\n\nThe diagram isn\u0027t clear about the source of the primitive color, so I looked at SkVertices.h: https://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:include/core/SkVertices.h;l\u003d122;drc\u003de49703faf265828903464f6a80a33e60f622cef0\n\nfColors says it has \"[vertexCount] or null\" elements. That makes me think that you get to set the primitive color on a per-vertex basis. So, if the primitive color is  used, it would need to be a varying, not a uniform.\n\nAfter looking at all of this stuff, I agree, `BlendColorFilterData` doesn\u0027t work, since it requires:\n- the output from the shader/paint-color stage (the \"priorStageOutput\")\n- a solid color uniform\n- blend mode (known)\n\nAlthough this is close, it\u0027s not a match. We can\u0027t represent the primitive color with a solid-color uniform since a uniform can\u0027t change on a per-vertex basis. So I guess we\u0027ll need to implement a new blend block which supports this.\n\n@michaelludwig, did I get this right? As you can see, I\u0027m not super familiar with the primitive blend stage.",
      "parentUuid": "bbf7b928_f68f6c2e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 74,
        "startChar": 74,
        "endLine": 74,
        "endChar": 81
      },
      "revId": "ca6652103b5a787457fcd311daeebe7c83f1d836",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
